        kind: 'faded',
        text: 'A metal plant has a board at the gate counting days without a lost-time injury, and a team bonus at every 100 days. Over two years, recordable injuries fell from 9 to 2 a year. In the same period, first-aid cases in the logbook rose from 30 to 55, and reported near misses fell from 120 to 40 a year. Headcount and hours stayed the same.',
        ask: 'What do you read in these numbers, and what do you propose?',
